Teach coding agents to use agent-cli. Commands: status, install [agent], remove [agent], show.
Install and remove require one agent or explicit --all. Agents need not be installed. No hooks, settings changes or instruction-file edits.
Supported agents: claude, codex, opencode, pi, omp, windsurf, cursor, gemini, antigravity.
User scope is the default (--user). --project uses the native agent path under the exact current directory, never a Git root.
User paths: Claude Code uses $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/skills or ~/.claude/skills; Antigravity uses ~/.gemini/config/skills; all others use ~/.agents/skills.
Project paths: Claude Code uses .claude/skills; all others use .agents/skills. Each path ends in the build's command name.
Agents sharing a directory share one skill: removing it affects every agent reading that directory.
For an agent without skill support, show --pointer prints text to paste yourself. show prints the full guide without installation.

Usage: agent-cli skill

Flags:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -v, --verbose  Print diagnostic details to stderr

Examples:
  agent-cli skill show
  agent-cli skill install codex
  agent-cli skill install --all --dry-run
  agent-cli skill status
  agent-cli skill remove codex

Environment: CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR (Claude user skill location only); no credentials or CLI config are read
Exit codes: 0 ok · 1 filesystem failure or conflict · 2 usage error or unknown agent
